Z||000000||fropuff||11-29-2001||11:54 PM||||Hey guys.  I'm thinking of what to get audio wise for my Fiero, and I was wondering a few things...<P>-If I get a CD burner for my computer, can I save the Internet-downloaded music to a .wav file?  I know it's easier to do a mp3 file, but I don't want to get a mp3 player.<P>-If I get a 6-disc add-on CD changer that connects with my stock FM stereo, will it work with the stock Fiero AM/FM/tape deck?<P>I think that's about it for now.  If I can remember anything else, I'll add to this.  Thanks a lot for any help.  I really appreciate it.  Have a good day!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||11-30-2001||12:01 AM||||Most CD-Burner software can switch back-and-forth with no issues... You don't need a HARDWARE MP3  player, just a software one to make sure you got the right/complete song...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Not sure that I follow the second Q... Elaborate/rephrase?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||11-30-2001||12:05 AM||||As for the second part, I was just wondering if the universal add-on CD changer with CD-R capabilities would work with my stock FM system, like they are supposed to.  Here's the one that I was thinking of: <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com/cgi-bin/S-veWJuBEunV5/ProdView.asp?s=0&c=3&g=610&I=130FM673&o=P&a=0" TARGET=_blank>http://www.crutchfield.com/cgi-bin/S-veWJuBEunV5/ProdView.asp?s=0&c=3&g=610&I=130FM673&o=P&a=0</A> <P>Thanks again for any help.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||11-30-2001||01:43 AM||||As to your second question, Yes it will work on any FM radio. It hooks into the antenna line. (You may need an adapter since there are 2 sizes. The Fiero uses the larger size and lots of new cars use the smaller size) ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||12-01-2001||01:55 AM||||Thanks for the help.  I was wondering if anyone has any recommendations for CD burners with software for switching to .wav files.  I'd think less than $150 is good for me.  Thanks again for any help.||||reg||1
